          "code": "import numpy as np\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(283)\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# First-Principles NumPy: Profit Curve P(tau), Lift@Top-K% & Instance-Dependent EV\n# Kasus: Deteksi Fraud Transaksi E-Commerce dengan nilai transaksi v_i log-normal (USD)\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nn = 4000\n# Nilai transaksi v_i berkisar lebar ($15 s.d. >$2.000)\ntx_value = np.round(rng.lognormal(mean=4.6, sigma=0.95, size=n), 2)\n# Probabilitas posterior fraud sejati (terkalibrasi): transaksi besar sedikit lebih rawan\nlogit = -3.6 + 0.45 * np.log1p(tx_value) - 1.8 + rng.normal(0.0, 1.35, size=n)\np_hat = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-logit))\ny_true = (rng.uniform(size=n) < p_hat).astype(int)\n\n# Struktur biaya/manfaat bisnis (USD) yang asimetris tinggi:\n# - Investigasi & gesekan nasabah saat memblokir/review (y_hat=1): c_review = $10, gesekan $6\n# - Jika fraud tertangkap (TP): menyelamatkan 90% nilai transaksi (0.90 * v_i) dikurangi c_review\n# - Jika transaksi sah diblokir (FP): rugi c_review + gesekan = -$16\nc_review = 10.0\nc_friction = 6.0\nrecovery_rate = 0.90\n\ndef eval_net_profit(y: np.ndarray, y_hat: np.ndarray, val: np.ndarray) -> float:\n    # Laba bersih relatif terhadap strategi 'tidak berbuat apa-apa' (baseline = 0):\n    # Menindak TP menyelamatkan (recovery_rate * v_i) dengan biaya c_review;\n    # Menindak FP membuang (c_review + c_friction)\n    saved_tp = np.sum(np.where((y == 1) & (y_hat == 1), recovery_rate * val - c_review, 0.0))\n    cost_fp = np.sum(np.where((y == 0) & (y_hat == 1), -(c_review + c_friction), 0.0))\n    return float(saved_tp + cost_fp)\n\n# 1) Ambang default tau = 0.50\ny_def = (p_hat >= 0.50).astype(int)\nprof_def = eval_net_profit(y_true, y_def, tx_value)\n\n# 2) Sapuan ambang global untuk Max-F1 vs Max-Profit Curve P(tau)\ngrid = np.linspace(0.02, 0.90, 89)\nbest_f1, tau_f1 = -1.0, 0.50\nbest_prof, tau_prof = -1e18, 0.50\nfor t in grid:\n    yh = (p_hat >= t).astype(int)\n    tp = int(np.sum((y_true == 1) & (yh == 1)))\n    fp = int(np.sum((y_true == 0) & (yh == 1)))\n    fn = int(np.sum((y_true == 1) & (yh == 0)))\n    f1 = (2 * tp) / (2 * tp + fp + fn) if (2 * tp + fp + fn) > 0 else 0.0\n    if f1 > best_f1:\n        best_f1, tau_f1 = f1, float(t)\n    pr = eval_net_profit(y_true, yh, tx_value)\n    if pr > best_prof:\n        best_prof, tau_prof = pr, float(t)\nprof_at_f1 = eval_net_profit(y_true, (p_hat >= tau_f1).astype(int), tx_value)\n\n# 3) Aturan Bayes Instance-Dependent: tindak jika E[Delta Profit | y_hat=1] > 0\n#    p_i * (0.85 * v_i - c_review) - (1 - p_i) * (c_review + c_friction) > 0\nev_gain = p_hat * (recovery_rate * tx_value - c_review) - (1.0 - p_hat) * (c_review + c_friction)\ny_ev = (ev_gain > 0.0).astype(int)\nprof_ev = eval_net_profit(y_true, y_ev, tx_value)\n\n# 4) Kendala Kapasitas Tim Analis: Top-5% Transaksi (K=200 tiket) -> Lift & Profit\nK = int(0.05 * n)\nidx_prob_top = np.argsort(-p_hat)[:K]\nidx_ev_top = np.argsort(-ev_gain)[:K]\ny_top_prob = np.zeros(n, dtype=int); y_top_prob[idx_prob_top] = 1\ny_top_ev = np.zeros(n, dtype=int); y_top_ev[idx_ev_top] = 1\nlift_top5 = (y_true[idx_prob_top].mean()) / y_true.mean()\ngain_top5 = y_true[idx_prob_top].sum() / y_true.sum()\n\nprint(f\"=== Profit Curves, Lift@Top-5% & Instance-Dependent EV (N={n}, Fraud={int(y_true.sum())}) ===\")\nprint(f\"1. Default Threshold (tau=0.50)         | Tiket={int(y_def.sum()):4d} | Net Savings = ${prof_def:10,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"2. Max-F1 Threshold  (tau={tau_f1:.2f}, F1={best_f1:.3f}) | Tiket={int((p_hat>=tau_f1).sum()):4d} | Net Savings = ${prof_at_f1:10,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"3. Optimal Global Profit (tau*={tau_prof:.2f})    | Tiket={int((p_hat>=tau_prof).sum()):4d} | Net Savings = ${best_prof:10,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"4. Instance-Dependent EV (p_i*v_i rule) | Tiket={int(y_ev.sum()):4d} | Net Savings = ${prof_ev:10,.2f}  <-- TERTINGGI!\")\nprint(f\"5. Capacity Top-5% (Sort Prob, K={K:3d})  | Lift={lift_top5:4.2f}x | CumGain={gain_top5:5.1%} | Net Savings = ${eval_net_profit(y_true, y_top_prob, tx_value):10,.2f}\")\nprint(f\"6. Capacity Top-5% (Sort EV,   K={K:3d})  | Tiket={K:4d} | Net Savings = ${eval_net_profit(y_true, y_top_ev, tx_value):10,.2f}\")",
          "expectedOutput": "=== Profit Curves, Lift@Top-5% & Instance-Dependent EV (N=4000, Fraud=274) ===\n1. Default Threshold (tau=0.50)         | Tiket=  31 | Net Savings = $  6,789.20\n2. Max-F1 Threshold  (tau=0.23, F1=0.362) | Tiket= 262 | Net Savings = $ 19,558.11\n3. Optimal Global Profit (tau*=0.11)    | Tiket= 763 | Net Savings = $ 23,585.96\n4. Instance-Dependent EV (p_i*v_i rule) | Tiket= 758 | Net Savings = $ 28,562.93  <-- TERTINGGI!\n5. Capacity Top-5% (Sort Prob, K=200)  | Lift=5.55x | CumGain=27.7% | Net Savings = $ 16,643.70\n6. Capacity Top-5% (Sort EV,   K=200)  | Tiket= 200 | Net Savings = $ 19,067.47",
          "actualOutput": "=== Profit Curves, Lift@Top-5% & Instance-Dependent EV (N=4000, Fraud=274) ===\n1. Default Threshold (tau=0.50)         | Tiket=  31 | Net Savings = $  6,789.20\n2. Max-F1 Threshold  (tau=0.23, F1=0.362) | Tiket= 262 | Net Savings = $ 19,558.11\n3. Optimal Global Profit (tau*=0.11)    | Tiket= 763 | Net Savings = $ 23,585.96\n4. Instance-Dependent EV (p_i*v_i rule) | Tiket= 758 | Net Savings = $ 28,562.93  <-- TERTINGGI!\n5. Capacity Top-5% (Sort Prob, K=200)  | Lift=5.55x | CumGain=27.7% | Net Savings = $ 16,643.70\n6. Capacity Top-5% (Sort EV,   K=200)  | Tiket= 200 | Net Savings = $ 19,067.47",
          "explanation": "Membangun kurva laba kumulatif dan Lift@Top-5% (5.55x) dari nol pada 4.000 transaksi bernilai log-normal: membuktikan hierarki penghematan bersih Default ($6.789) < Max-F1 ($19.558) < Optimal Global Profit ($23.586) < Instance-Dependent EV ($28.563 dengan tiket lebih sedikit!).",
          "verificationStatus": "VERIFIED_RUNNABLE",
          "isVerifiedOutput": true,
